    {
      "type": "tweet",
      "id": "2002708058145792210",
      "url": "https://x.com/Gavel_on_X/status/2002708058145792210",
      "twitterUrl": "https://twitter.com/Gavel_on_X/status/2002708058145792210",
      "text": "📢 STOP TO AI FANTASY!📢: YouTube’s Hard Line on Synthetic Content\n\nYouTube is taking a definitive stand on the wave of AI-generated content flooding the platform. In a major policy shift, the focus is moving away from \"AI for the sake of AI\" and toward transparency, realism, and educational value.\n\n🔍 The \"Real vs. Synthetic\" Threshold\nYouTube now mandates that creators disclose when realistic-looking content has been created or altered using AI. This isn't just about labels; it’s about trust. If a video looks real but is synthetic, the audience has a right to know.\n\n🎓 Educational Value is the New Gold Standard\nThe platform is tightening its grip on \"low-effort\" AI fantasy content. Moving forward, AI-generated material that deals with sensitive topics will be judged through the EDSA lens:\n\n- Educational\n\n- Documentary\n\n- Scientific\n\n- Artistic\n\nPurely \"imaginary\" AI content that mimics reality without providing tangible educational utility or a clear artistic purpose faces stricter scrutiny, reduced reach, or removal.\n\n🛡️ Why This Matters\nThis decision marks a turning point in the battle against misinformation. By prioritizing content that teaches, informs, or documents—rather than just simulates—YouTube is ensuring that the next generation of digital media remains a tool for learning, not just a hall of mirrors.\n\n\"Innovation must be balanced with responsibility. We are prioritizing AI that adds value to the human experience, not content that replaces truth with fiction.\"\n\nWHAT DO YOU THINK?👇\n\n#YouTubeUpdate #ArtificialIntelligence #ContentCreators #DigitalEthics #TechNews2025",
      "source": "Twitter for iPhone",
      "retweetCount": 0,
      "replyCount": 1,
      "likeCount": 2,
